## The bus shelter

::bg{location="marrow_bay_bus_shelter" time="morning"}
::music{action="start" mood="wistful" volume="down"}
@narrator: The last stop on the coast road is a shelter with no walls, only a roof and a timetable nobody has updated since spring.
@sol{mono}: Seven days. Aunt Pell said seven days, and then the festival, and then the bus home.
::auto{character="pell" anchor="center" action="fadeInUp"}
::set{run.seen.pell = run.day}
@pell{emotion="happy"}: There you are! You've grown a whole head. Give me that bag before the gulls do.
@sol: Hi, Aunt Pell.
@pell{emotion="teasing" when="has(prev.run.lantern.paper) && !prev.run.lantern.paper"}: And this summer we find the paper first. I've written it on my hand. Look. PAPER.

## The lantern shop

::bg{location="lantern_shop" time="morning"}
::auto{character="pell" anchor="left" action="fadeInUp"}
@narrator: The shop smells of glue and salt. Paper lanterns hang from every beam like sleeping bats.
@pell: Friday night is the Lantern Walk. Every household sends one lantern out on the tide.
@pell{emotion="tired"}: And this year my hands shake too much to fold the frame.
<branch id="help" prompt="Aunt Pell looks at you over her glasses.">
  <choice id="yes" label="I'll make the lantern.">
    ::accept{quest="festivalLantern"}
    @pell{emotion="happy"}: I knew you would. You'll want reed for the frame and good paper. The library girl knows paper.
  </choice>
  <choice id="maybe" label="I've never made one...">
    ::accept{quest="festivalLantern"}
    @pell{emotion="teasing"}: Nobody has, until they have. Ask at the library for paper. Theo at the pier cuts reed.
  </choice>
</branch>
::auto{character="pell" action="fadeOut"}
@sol{mono}: Friday. Four days to build something that floats.
